WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.217
The product totals common table expression creates one row per department and product.

00:00:06.217 --> 00:00:13.232
The ranked common table expression keeps the same grain but adds dense rank within each department.

00:00:13.232 --> 00:00:18.457
The final select statement filters to the top two rank groups.

00:00:18.457 --> 00:00:23.187
Run the query and trace the grain through all three stages.

00:00:23.187 --> 00:00:27.062
This is a strong example of readable advanced S Q L.
